 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Nuh: no motif, no figure. Their claim (60:5-9) is framed «ردوا عليه أقبح رد». 59:15-20 not glossed (which day is meant is not settled). A ship for «فأنجيناه… في الفلك», leaving before «وأغرقنا»; no drowning drawn. Geometric for «اعبدوا الله ما لكم من إله غيره». STAGING v4: Nuh is a blue drop labelled Nuh, never a figure; no motif on his name. His people's chiefs are three faceless men in dark robes in a town (the place is not named by the sources, so a plain town). c1 (59-62): Nuh speaks on 59:6, geometric on 59:8-14 (worship Allah), the camera on them for the warning (59:16); the chiefs answer (60:1), the camera on them, they shake their heads on 60:8 (clear error); Nuh answers (61:1, 62:1), a seal plate for the messages of his Lord (62:1-3). c2 (63-64): Nuh speaks (63:1), a light plate for the reminder (63:4-8, held wide), the camera on them for the warning (63:10); on 64:1 (they denied him) they turn away and leave on 64:2, so nobody is on the stage at the flood. The ark comes in on 64:3 and Nuh moves to it (64:3-6, saved with those with him in the ark: the believers inside are not drawn, so they are not counted); the flood rises over the empty town from 64:7 and the ark floats, Nuh's drop above the water. Nobody is drowned or hurt; no ruin. Time is day, not dawn."
 },
